1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,375
Build the part with FreeCAD's parametric cylinder controls.

2
00:00:07,375 --> 00:00:10,750
Enter a 20 mm radius for the 40 mm flange.

3
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:14,125
Make the flange 6 mm thick at the default origin.

4
00:00:14,125 --> 00:00:18,500
Confirm the cylinder to create the flange solid.

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,875
Use a second additive cylinder with a 12 mm radius.

6
00:00:21,875 --> 00:00:25,250
Set height to 30 mm while retaining the origin placement.

7
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:30,625
The shaft joins the flange as a single solid.

8
00:00:30,625 --> 00:00:34,000
Set a 6 mm radius for a 12 mm through bore.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,375
Use a 30 mm subtractive cylinder along the Z axis.

10
00:00:37,375 --> 00:00:42,750
Confirm the cut and inspect the central opening.

11
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:47,125
The final feature retains its 6 mm radius and 30 mm height.

12
00:00:47,125 --> 00:00:50,500
Store the complete parametric feature history in FCStd format.

13
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:53,875
The saved document is named flanged-bushing.

14
00:00:53,875 --> 00:00:57,250
Export the final solid for use in other CAD software.

15
00:00:57,250 --> 00:01:00,625
Save flanged-bushing.step alongside the native document.

16
00:01:00,625 --> 00:01:05,000
Accept the native STEP settings to write the exchange model.

17
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:15,375
Native and STEP checks confirm one valid solid, 40 × 40 × 30 mm bounds, and the through bore.
